# Demo viewer (127.0.0.1:9891)

When you finish work under `demo/`, change viewer behavior, or tell the user to open `http://127.0.0.1:9891/`, **ensure the static server is running** so they do not see “connection refused”.

1. Check: `curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" http://127.0.0.1:9891/` — expect `200`.
2. If not `200`, from the **repository root** start in the background (survives tool timeout):

   `nohup python3 -m http.server 9891 --directory demo >> /tmp/atelier-demo-9891.log 2>&1 & sleep 1`

   (Equivalent for humans: `npm run demo` — foreground.)

3. Then tell the user the URL (e.g. `http://127.0.0.1:9891/?repo=pydantic-ai`).
